    content: "Read the following passages carefully before proceeding:\n\n\"Isaiah also cries out concerning Israel: 'Though the number of the children of Israel be as the sand of the sea, the remnant will be saved.'\" — Romans 9:27 (NKJV)\n\n\"Even so then, at this present time there is a remnant according to the election of grace.\" — Romans 11:5 (NKJV)\n\n\"Knowing that you were not redeemed with corruptible things, like silver or gold, from your aimless conduct received by tradition from your fathers, but with the precious blood of Christ, as of a lamb without blemish and without spot.\" — 1 Peter 1:18-19 (NKJV)\n\nAs you read, notice Paul's emphasis on grace as the basis of the remnant's existence. Consider how Peter's reminder of redemption by blood — not by heritage or tradition — shapes the posture the remnant should carry.",
